response:
Acupuncture is considered a pseudoscientific therapy that may help in treating certain conditions, including migraines. If you’re considering using this treatment, be aware of its risks as well as benefits.

The benefits include:

- Improved circulation;
- A release of endorphins and other natural pain-killing chemicals in the brain (neurotransmitters);
- Stimulation of the body’s natural healing abilities;
- Prevention or reversal of unwanted symptoms;
- Increased energy levels;
- Better sleep quality;
- Emotional healing.

However, the risks should not be ignored. These include:

- Infection at needle points;
- Minor bleeding or bruising post-treatment;
- Nerve damage when done improperly.

To use acupuncture alongside your existing care, make sure you discuss this option with your healthcare provider before starting any sessions. Your practitioner should be experienced and certified, and you must communicate any adverse effects immediately. Always remember to take a balanced approach: stick to scientifically proven treatments first, and rely on acupuncture for additional support only.
